      <memberdef kind="function" id="classthemis_1_1performance_1_1_intelligent_prefetcher_1af5cf5d45f463a6b881a9eb59957ba922" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void themis::performance::IntelligentPrefetcher::record_access</definition>
        <argsstring>(uint64_t address, uint64_t timestamp=0)</argsstring>
        <name>record_access</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::performance::IntelligentPrefetcher::record_access</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>uint64_t</type>
          <declname>address</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint64_t</type>
          <declname>timestamp</declname>
          <defval>0</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Record a memory access and update the pattern model. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Record access.</para>
<para>This is the primary training input for the learning engine. Each call appends <computeroutput>address</computeroutput> to the sliding history window and re-fits the dominant stride. When an address matches a prior prediction the useful_prefetches counter is incremented (feedback loop).</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>address</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>64-bit address of the accessed memory location. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>timestamp</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Access timestamp (nanoseconds since epoch, or any monotonic counter). Used to adapt prefetch distance.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">address</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input parameter. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">timestamp</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input parameter.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Implements record_access without additional internal calls. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
