        <briefdescription>
<para>Predict the next <computeroutput>lookahead</computeroutput> addresses after <computeroutput>current_address</computeroutput>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Predict next accesses.</para>
<para>Uses the learned stride to extrapolate future addresses. Only predictions that exceed the configured confidence threshold are returned.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>current_address</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The address from which to project. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>lookahead</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Maximum number of future addresses to return. Capped at <computeroutput>max_prefetch_distance</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Ordered vector of predicted addresses (may be empty when confidence is too low or the history is insufficient).</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">current_address</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input parameter. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">lookahead</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input parameter. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Return value.</para>
</simplesect>
Implements predict_next_accesses without additional internal calls. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
