    <briefdescription>
<para>Intelligent Prefetching System (v1.8.0). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Machine learning-based prefetcher that learns memory access patterns and proactively loads data to reduce cache miss latency.</para>
<para>Research basis: &quot;Learning-based Prefetching&quot; (MICRO&apos;19).</para>
<para>Features:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Pattern Learning: detects sequential and strided access patterns via a sliding window of recent addresses.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Prefetch Distance: adaptively adjusts the number of addresses to prefetch ahead based on observed access latency.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Confidence Scoring: only prefetches when the pattern confidence exceeds the configured threshold.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Multi-Level: routes prefetch requests to L1, L2, L3, or DRAM (non-temporal) based on confidence level.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Feedback Loop: records hit/miss outcomes to improve accuracy estimates reported in <ref refid="structthemis_1_1performance_1_1_intelligent_prefetcher_1_1_prefetch_stats" kindref="compound">PrefetchStats</ref>.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Thread safety: all public methods are protected by an internal mutex and are safe to call concurrently. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
